  "body": "## What changed\n\nControl-side cutter compensation (both COMP variants: control = part contour, wear = centre path) now posts on three more mill dialects, each in its own words:\n\n- **Haas** - `G1 G41|G42 X.. Y.. Z.. D<tool> F..` on the lead-in, `G1 G40 ..` on the lead-out (D = the tool's offset row, the H word's row).\n- **Mazak (EIA/ISO)** - `G01 G41|G42 .. D<tool>`, `G01 G40`.\n- **Siemens 840D** - `G1 G41|G42 NORM ..`, no D word: the radius is the active edge the tool call already selected (`T n D n`); NORM is stated so a modal KONT can never move the engage point.\n\nThe Fanuc post's laws carry over unchanged: a comp word that would land on a rapid, an arc, or survive to the section end, or a comp record inside a canned cycle, is a named counted refusal that blocks the gate. Wear writes one register note per section.\n\n**Heidenhain keeps its by-name refusal** (message now names the posts that do support it): the TNC's documented engage point (\"perpendicular to the programmed position\") is not stated against the next element the way the Fanuc start-up is, so a perpendicular lead's engage point would be a guess; and the TNC always offsets by R + DR, so wear's \"register holds only the delta\" has no TNC form. Tormach is out of scope and still refuses. Reasoning in `docs/decisions/39-comp-dialects.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\nHaas mill operator's manual (G41/G42 need a Dnnn; Setting 58 Fanuc/Yasnac changes outside-corner joins only), Siemens 840D sl Programming Manual Fundamentals (\"Contour approach and retraction\": NORM, perpendicular to the path tangent at the start point; T/D edge selection), Heidenhain TNC 640 ISO programming manual (G41/G42 in a G01 block, radius R + DR, comp effective at block end), RS-274 / ISO 6983. Behaviour only.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-post --test comp`: `haas_mazak_and_840d_write_their_words_on_the_leads`, `haas_mazak_and_840d_refuse_a_comp_word_on_an_arc_a_rapid_or_the_section_end`, `every_wear_post_notes_the_register_once_and_control_writes_no_note`, `every_other_shipped_post_refuses_control_compensation_by_name` (now Heidenhain, lathe, Tormach)\n- `camcraft-app --test control_comp`: `haas_mazak_and_840d_post_the_part_contour_under_their_own_comp_words_to_the_goldens` (goldens `golden/nc/{haas,mazak,sinumerik}/contour_control_comp.nc`, gate releases)\n- `camcraft-app --test wear_comp`: `haas_mazak_and_840d_post_wear_over_the_centre_path_to_the_goldens` (goldens `golden/nc/{haas,mazak,sinumerik}/contour_wear_comp.nc`)\n\nGate: camcraft-post all suites green; app control_comp, wear_comp, conformance, fanuc_post, cli, arc_planes, drill_rplane, probe_op, heidenhain_arc_centre, heidenhain_block_form, vertical_arc_entry green; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. Comp-free goldens byte-identical.\n\nChangelog: Haas, Mazak and Siemens 840D posts write G41/G42/G40 cutter compensation (control and wear); Heidenhain still refuses by name\n\nFixes #39\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
